# What must never reach a build context.
#
# It lives at the REPOSITORY ROOT because that is the build context
# (`docker build -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile .`): Docker only reads the
# `.dockerignore` at the root of the context, so a copy next to the Dockerfile
# would be silently ignored.
#
# A context is copied to the daemon, so a large directory is a slow build — and a
# SECRETS file that reaches a context is a secret in a layer's history, which no
# later `rm` removes.

# State. The image contains no data; `/data` is the volume.
**/data/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/sessions/
**/backups/
**/scratch/

# Secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
**/secrets.env
**/state/*/secrets.env

# Build output and tooling caches: rebuilt in the image.
**/node_modules/
**/lib/
**/dist/
.tooling/
cache/
**/.pnpm-store/
**/.npm/

# Development and tests.
**/test/
**/*.test.ts
**/coverage/
.git/
.github/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Editors.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
